    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Look.</strong> Silas's second wife, 40s. Sharp cheekbones, black-feathered swan mask and gown, a fan she snaps shut when annoyed. Stable mud on her hem.</p><p><strong>Wants.</strong> Out of a cold marriage; to leave at dawn with a lover who signs his letters 'R.'</p><p><strong>Secret.</strong> Her packed trunk is in a carriage in the stables and R.'s love letter (C12) is tucked in her glove. She spent 8:30-9:00 loading the carriage.</p><p><strong>Knows.</strong> At about 8:45, from the stable yard, she saw a green glow moving past the chapel windows. Shares it once her secret is safe (Persuasion DC 14, or the letter plus a promise of discretion).</p><p><strong>Plays as.</strong> Clipped and haughty; softens only when treated with respect.</p><p><strong>Lines.</strong></p><ul><li>“I was in my room. With a headache. Which you are now giving me.”</li><li>“If I tell you what I saw, my business stays my own. Agreed?”</li></ul>",
        "public": ""
      },
